# Transcript documents of another person's published lectures, held for private
# research only (CCW-B7 "What NOT to do"). This repository pushes to GitHub, so
# they stay on disk and out of the history.
#
# ⚠ This rule lives at report_run level as well as in sources/youtube/, because
# the documents are in THREE directories, not one. Counted on disk 30 Aug:
#
#   docs/report_run/                       7  THE STARKEY THESIS *.docx
#   docs/report_run/sources/               2  David Starkey.docx, Restoration and Repeal ...
#   docs/report_run/sources/youtube/       7  the same seven again
#
# CCW-B8 step 1 put the rule in sources/youtube/.gitignore, which governs that
# directory and below. THIS rule is the only cover for the nine in the first two
# directories — it is not a backstop for the sources/youtube copies, which have
# their own nearer rule.
#
# ⚠ Verify location with `find`, never with `git check-ignore`. check-ignore
# resolves a PATHNAME against the rules whether or not a file is there, so it
# will happily attribute a rule to a path that does not exist — and reading its
# attribution as evidence of where the files are gets the layout wrong. Both
# facts below were established separately: `find -maxdepth 1 -name '*.docx'` for
# existence, `check-ignore -v` for the rule. All 16 come back ignored, and
# nothing had been committed.
#
# Charlie: if these should be backed up, R2 is the right home, not git.
*.docx

# Corpus search exports (CCW-B9) — derived from the same private corpus.
starkey_hits.json
register_candidates.json
register_candidates_full.json
